DESCRIPTION:What is TinkerCAD and what can you do with it?\n\nTinkerCAD is 
 a browser-based software that allows you to create\, composite\, and edit 
 3D files using existing 3D files or drawing from a library of customizable
  shapes. \n\n \n\nCourse Description\n\nThis course will take students thr
 ough an overview of TinkerCAD using Makerspace lab computers. Students wil
 l be able to follow along with Makerspace Staff to create 3D assets. Befor
 e the course\, students should create a free account here: https://www.tin
 kercad.com/\n\n \n\nCourse Goals and Objectives\n\nThe goal of the course 
 is to have students develop and enrich their understanding of TinkerCAD to
  be able to create 3D files for use in 3D printing or design. At the end o
 f the course\, students will be able to:\n\nCreate and open TinkerCAD proj
 ects\,Design and Manipulate 3D assets in the editor\,Explore tools and fun
 ctionalities within the software\,Understand Isometric angles and export a
 ppropriately framed snapshots.
GEO:33.210068;-97.148954
LOCATION:Willis Library\, The Spark Makerspace Willis Library
SUMMARY:TinkerCAD Workshop
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unt.edu/event/tinkercad-workshop
CATEGORIES:Workshops & Training
END:VEVENT
