DESCRIPTION:What is Adobe Illustrator and what can you do with it?\n\nAdobe
  Illustrator is an industry-standard graphic design software that allows u
 sers to create drawings\, illustrations\, and artwork. Adobe Illustrator o
 ffers a wide range of tools that enable designers to create shapes\, graph
 ics\, illustrations\, compositions\, and mock-ups with ease. Designers can
  trace shapes from existing images\, manipulate text in fun and exciting w
 ays\, re-color or apply filters or effects to images\, or make eye-catchin
 g product displays and mock-ups.\n\nIn addition\, Adobe Illustrator enable
 s designers to create vector graphics\, which allow for the image or objec
 t to be resized without loss of quality. This provides advantages for desi
 gners interested in large prints\, marketing graphics\, or laser cuts and 
 engraves.\n\n \n\nCourse Description\n\nThis course\, led by student staff
  at The Spark\, will demonstrate various applications and techniques for u
 sing Adobe Illustrator for beginners. Students will be able to follow alon
 g on our workspace computers and ask questions.\n\n \n\nCourse Goals and O
 bjectives\n\nThe goal of the course is to have students develop and enrich
  their understanding of Adobe Illustrator to be able to use the software f
 or a variety of graphic applications. By the end of the course\, students 
 will be able to:\n\nCreate and open Adobe Illustrator projects\,Import ima
 ge files into Adobe Illustrator\,Manipulate existing or imported image fil
 es on a basic level\,Manipulate text in the Illustrator workspace\, andExp
 ort finished Adobe Illustrator projects into useable image files.
GEO:33.210068;-97.148954
LOCATION:Willis Library\, The Spark Makerspace Willis Library
SUMMARY:Adobe Illustrator Workshop
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unt.edu/event/adobe-illustrator-workshop
